Done — committed as e5f89637, working tree clean.

## What landed

Step 1 (#815) — `/spawn replay` no longer silently drops `--pr`:

• build_spawn_manifest(run_id, tasks, results, pr) now emits `"pr": pr, threaded from the launching SpawnArgs.pr at the one --parallel` call site.
• ParsedManifest gained pr: bool, read defensively: .get("pr").and_then(as_bool).unwrap_or(false).
• The replay arm passes pr: manifest.pr instead of the hardcoded false.
• New pure `replay_banner(run_id, task_count, created_ts, pr)` — a replay about to open draft PRs says so *on the line announcing the replay*, before it acts. With `pr: false` the string is byte-identical to the pre-#815 banner.

Five tests, both directions plus the near-miss (a discriminator tested only on the side that fires is vacuous green): `pr: true round-trips true, pr: false round-trips false, a legacy JSON with **no** pr key parses to false with its tasks intact, the banner names --pr when set, and the no-pr` banner is asserted as an exact string.

The unwrap_or(false) is deliberate and documented in both the struct field and the parser: pre-#815 manifests genuinely recorded no modifier, so false is the honest reading of that absence rather than a guess.

Step 2 — register drift paid off, done first as instructed:

